    "28": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Form tracker",
          "heading": "Fiji overcome Canada in home clash during latest tournament appearance",
          "body": "Fiji recorded a 45-29 victory against Canada in their most recent fixture, which took place at home in September 2026 during the Pacific Nations Cup knockout stage. Across their last five international matches, the Flying Fijians have secured two victories. During this same five-game span, the side also suffered three defeats. This run leaves the squad seeking greater consistency ahead of their next fixture."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "CONTRACT BACKLASH",
          "heading": "Stuart Barnes slams RFU ‘ostrich policy’ after Steve Borthwick receives contract extension",
          "body": "Former England fly-half Stuart Barnes has criticised the RFU’s 'ostrich policy' after the governing body extended Steve Borthwick’s contract until 2028. Writing for The Times, Barnes described the head coach’s tenure as a 'failure' following a Six Nations campaign that featured a historic loss to Italy. While England recently concluded their summer schedule with a 31-24 victory over Argentina, Barnes insists the side has slipped to 'second-tier' status. The RFU maintains the extension provides vital continuity as preparations for the 2027 World Cup in Australia intensify."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "RANKINGS HISTORY",
          "heading": "France held the world number one ranking for one single week",
          "body": "Les Bleus occupied the world number one ranking for a solitary week in July 2022, representing their longest unbroken spell at the summit. This seven-day window remains the historical benchmark for the national side in the top position without interruption. France currently sit third in the Nations Championship log after three fixtures, having scored 116 points and conceded 75. A 42-15 victory over Japan in Round 3 secured their second win of the tournament."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "FIXTURE STANCE",
          "heading": "IRFU rejects Alan Gilpin proposal to move Six Nations matches to USA",
          "body": "The Irish Rugby Football Union has dismissed suggestions of relocating future Six Nations fixtures to the United States, following comments from World Rugby chief executive Alan Gilpin. While Gilpin highlighted the commercial potential of hosting an Ireland versus Italy clash in New York or Boston, an IRFU spokesperson insisted there are \"currently no plans or discussions\" regarding such a move. The union emphasised that home matches remain a central part of the competition's appeal for fans in Ireland and Italy."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "FIXTURE PROPOSAL",
          "heading": "Italy and Ireland fixture move to United States stalled by IRFU stance",
          "body": "Today's coverage provides no further progress on the potential relocation of the Azzurri's championship meeting with Ireland to North America. Although World Rugby recently floated the plan to expand the game's reach in the United States, the IRFU clarified in recent reports that it has no immediate plans to move home games. The situation remains an open discussion point for tournament organisers, but no official change in stance has been confirmed today."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "BALL TRIAL",
          "heading": "World Rugby expands size-4.5 ball trial despite 'worst decision' player backlash",
          "body": "World Rugby is expanding the trial of the smaller size-4.5 ball across the international game, according to reports today, despite increasing vocal opposition from several Test players. While governing bodies suggest the change assists handling and kicking range, some athletes have labelled the move the \"worst decision ever\" for the sport's professional development. The update follows Saturday's 64-26 opening WXV defeat for Scotland against Canada, where the hosts struggled to contain a clinical ten-try performance in Edinburgh."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Return nears",
          "heading": "Taulupe Faletau targets Cardiff return to bolster Wales’ autumn back-row options",
          "body": "Taulupe Faletau is nearing a competitive return for Cardiff, with the club optimistic the veteran No. 8 will be fit for the start of the United Rugby Championship. After being sidelined by injury and missing the recent international window, the back-rower’s progress is being closely monitored ahead of the season opener. A successful comeback for his region would provide a vital experienced option for Wales as they look to recover from a difficult run of results in the Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "SCORING DATA",
          "heading": "Los Pumas concede 31.5 points on average across their last 11 tests",
          "body": "Argentina have averaged 29.2 points scored and 31.5 conceded throughout their last 11 matches. During this window, Los Pumas have registered 321 points in total while surrendering 346 to their opponents. The standout result remains the 52-28 victory over Wales in November 2025, which stands as the team’s largest winning margin of the period. These figures highlight a high-scoring trend for the national side ahead of the upcoming November internationals."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "POSITIONAL DEBATE",
          "heading": "Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii rejects calls to specialise despite mounting Rugby World Cup pressure",
          "body": "Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii has dismissed suggestions he must settle on one position to maximise his impact before the 2027 home tournament. The 23-year-old code-switcher insisted he maintains an “open mindset” regarding his role, despite James Slipper’s warning that Australia must find a way to get the ball into his hands more often. This comes as Les Kiss faces mounting selection dilemmas, compounded by fly-half Carter Gordon being sidelined with a broken leg following the recent international series in Argentina."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tournament final",
          "heading": "Japan sets up Pacific Nations Cup final showdown against defending champions",
          "body": "Japan will contest the Pacific Nations Cup final after a comprehensive 63-14 victory over the United States in Saturday’s semifinal in Osaka. The Brave Blossoms controlled the encounter at Hanazono Rugby Stadium, building on their status as favourites against the Americans. They now move on to face two-time defending champion Fiji at Prince Chichibu Memorial Stadium. Fiji earned their place in the decider by defeating Canada 45-29 in their own semifinal earlier on the same day."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugby Asia 247"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Officiating frustration",
          "heading": "Neil Barnes slams referee after All Blacks lose series to Springboks",
          "body": "All Blacks senior assistant coach Neil Barnes has hit out at referee Karl Dickson following the 43-28 loss in Baltimore. Barnes claimed the world champions received “penalties for bugger all” which allowed South Africa to dictate the pace of the final Test. The defeat confirmed a 3-1 series triumph for the Springboks, leaving the All Blacks to reflect on a series where they were repeatedly outmuscled. Barnes insisted his side remains “seriously close” to the Boks despite the final scoreline."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "467": {
      "date": "2026-09-14",
      "edition": "Monday 14 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Series triumph",
          "heading": "South Africa secure series victory over New Zealand in Baltimore Test",
          "body": "The Springboks completed a dominant 3-1 series win over New Zealand after a 43-28 victory in Saturday's fourth Test. Damian de Allende crossed twice while Morne van den Berg, Pieter-Steph du Toit, Kurt-Lee Arendse, and Cameron Hanekom also scored in front of 68,173 fans. Siya Kolisi praised Rassie Erasmus’ influence, noting, “He knows how to get us up, and when he speaks to us he reminds us where we come from.” The result cements South Africa's status as the team to beat."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    }
  }
}